I arrived in Odense a little past nine.
I left the station and walked directly toward the old quarter.
The sun was shining, and I enjoyed the fresh spring air.
After a short walk, the city changed.
Suddenly I stood on a narrow street with cobblestones.
The cobblestones were worn and old.
I looked at the many small houses.
They lay close together in a row along the street.
Almost all the houses were funny and very crooked.
Each house showed its very own personality.
Many of them were painted in beautiful, bright colors.
I especially noticed the yellow and red houses.
The colorful walls lit up in the spring sun.
I simply loved the old part of town.
I stood and looked at the crooked houses for a long time.
Each house had its own cheerful colour.
I wanted to remember this street forever.
After that, I slowly walked further down the street.
